  "slug": "elegans-lifespan-0bcf",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published study test how diet, temperature, drugs and neuropeptides change C. elegans lifespan and proteotoxicity.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that lifespan and healthspan outcomes in C. elegans depend on context, including temperature, diet and the stress-pathway branch engaged. Dietary human HSP90 supplied via E. coli extends lifespan and healthspan through DAF-16, SKN-1 and HSF-1 stress signaling. Developmental daf-2 knockdown extends lifespan at 15°C but not 25°C, and the requirement for skn-1 is temperature-dependent. Methionine restriction extends lifespan through intestinal UPRmt activation that requires PKC-1 and the neuropeptides INS-27, INS-34 and INS-35. Rapamycin delays amyloid-β-induced paralysis and extends survival in C. elegans Alzheimer's models without reducing amyloid burden. The items test different interventions and do not describe a single mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
